<p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"=
><span>That means they are obliged to pay whatever price U.S. wheat goes fo=
r, even if it is substantially higher than what other countries are offerin=
g. Analysts in Bangladesh have denounced the deal as unfair.</span></p><p s=
tyle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><sp=
an>The one saving grace this year is that the world had a bumper crop of wh=
eat in 2025. There is still leftover grain stored in the silos of farmers, =
traders and government reserves.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25p=
x georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But the year should serve=
 as a wake-up call, experts say. The world is enormously dependent on a han=
dful of breadbaskets; when something goes wrong, there are few other option=
s.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;mar=
gin:0 0 15px"><span>=E2=80=9CIt is na=C3=AFve to think we can rely on a foo=
